DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Professor Riccardo Crescenzi \, London School of Econo
 mics\nSt Catharine's Political Economy Seminar Series\nTopics: Law\, Polit
 ics\, Policy\nDetails: https://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273723/\nSpeaker
 : -Professor Riccardo Crescenzi \n Talk Title: tbc\n Time: 18:00 -19:30 \n
  Location: Ramsden room\, St Catharine's College \n The seminar series is 
 supported by the Cambridge Political Economy Society and the Economics and
  Policy Group at the Cambridge Judge Business School. \n\n Talk Overview: 
 tbc\n\n Speaker Overview: \n Riccardo Crescenzi is a Professor of Economic
  Geography at the London School of Economics and Political Science (LSE)\,
  UK. He has been a European Research Council (ERC) grant holder\, leading 
 a major five-year research project on foreign direct investment (FDI)\, gl
 obal value chains (GVCs) and their territorial impacts across the globe. H
 e is currently the LSE Principal Investigator of a large collaborative res
 earch project funded by Horizon Europe and UK Research and Innovation (UKR
 I) on inequalities in the era of global megatrends.
END:VEVENT
